body:
BUG: Labels not programmatically associated with inputs (WCAG 4.1.2 Fail)

Filed by: GD — ARIA audit of exam.html post-FR fix

SEVERITY: P2 — Accessibility regression. Affects screen reader users on ALL exam questions.

PROBLEM
In renderInput() (exam.html ~line 401-436), label elements are NOT linked to their inputs via for/id:

  dropdown (line 405): html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';
  number   (line 414): html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';
  text     (line 432): html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';

Screen readers require for="inputId" to announce the label when the input receives focus.
Without it, VoiceOver/NVDA announces only the placeholder or nothing.

WCAG: SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships) Level A, SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value) Level A

FIX — 3 lines changed in renderInput()

1. Dropdown (line 405):
   BEFORE: html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';
   AFTER:  html += '<label for="' + inp.id + '">' + inp.label + '</label>';

2. Number (line 414):
   BEFORE: html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';
   AFTER:  html += '<label for="' + inp.id + '">' + inp.label + '</label>';

3. Text (line 432):
   BEFORE: html += '<label>' + inp.label + '</label>';
   AFTER:  html += '<label for="' + inp.id + '">' + inp.label + '</label>';

SECONDARY: Canvas elements in renderGraph() (line 442) have no aria-label.
Add role='img' and aria-label to canvas:
  BEFORE: html += '<canvas id="' + g.canvas_id + '" width="500" height="500"></canvas>';
  AFTER:  html += '<canvas id="' + g.canvas_id + '" width="500" height="500" role="img" aria-label="Graph for question ' + (g.title || g.canvas_id) + '"></canvas>';

The canvas label can be simple -- it just needs SOMETHING for screen readers that encounter graph questions.

VERIFY
After fix: focus any exam input with VoiceOver/NVDA -- it should announce both the label text AND the input type.
E.g. "Enter the slope: text field" (not just "text field").

SCOPE: exam.html only. 3-4 line change in renderInput() + 1 line in renderGraph().
